            "review_title": "Review at SalaThai",
            "review_text": "Michael T\n4 contributions\n0\nDisappointing Sala Thai\nDec 2025 • Solo\nRecently went to the Sala Thai Restaurant in the Old Quarter, Hanoi. The place itself was clean and I enjoyed the surroundings. The staff as usual being Vietnamese were gracious and congenial. I ordered the vegetarian Tom Yum Soup and the vegetarian Pad Thai. The soup arrived in short order and although it was tasty and spicy and a large portion - especially for one - there wasn't that many vegetables and mostly disappointing was there wasn't any tofu. With the price of the soup you thought they would have put at least one protein in the soup. Much of the ingredients were also inedible, i.e. lemongrass and galanga. The soup was in a very lovely bowl and heated with a candle underneath - very nice. Now for the Pad Thai. I had finished the soup and 20 minutes later the PT still hadn't arrived. One of the servers - a lovely senior lady - mentioned that the PT would be arriving soon. 15-20 minutes later it still hadn't arrived and when it did the server tried serving it to the gentleman next to me who had arrived 30 mins after I had sat down. The Pad Thai was quite a small portion and again no tofu and a small amount of vegetables. A few pieces each of carrots, celery, and daikon. Having said that the PT was tasty and spicy; but for the price - not cheap - I was expecting much better. Having to wait 30 mins maybe more for a signature Thai dish seems to be ridiculous. The restaurant wasn't especially busy so they couldn't use that as an excuse. I believe they were also hoping for a tip as they handed me the bill in one of those leather folders where diners usually leave a tip when they do. I honestly could not leave a tip and if I did it would have bothered me for the rest of the night. Maybe the non-vegetarians fare better; but I definitely would not return.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nMy first time at this restaurant; but many just a bad day. Maybe their primary chef called in sick.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 27, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
